              <li><strong><a href="/headstones/bevel-markers" class="text-bronze font-medium underline hover:text-evergreen transition-colors">Bevel markers</a></strong> — the quiet middle option. Slight raised profile. A good choice for families who don't want a visible upright signaling absence during summer months back east.</li>
              <li><strong><a href="/headstones/companion-headstones" class="text-bronze font-medium underline hover:text-evergreen transition-colors">Companion / double headstones</a></strong> — one monument, two lives. Common for snowbird retiree couples where one spouse has passed and the other is planning ahead.</li>
              <li><strong><a href="/headstones/bronze-memorials" class="text-bronze font-medium underline hover:text-evergreen transition-colors">Bronze markers</a></strong> — the dominant marker type at Southern Utah National Cemetery. Also available for private cemeteries with VA medallion.</li>
