              <li><strong>Manufacture and laser etch:</strong> 6–12 weeks depending on granite availability and engraving complexity. Temple silhouettes and photorealistic laser etches take the longer end of that range.</li>
              <li><strong>Freight and setting:</strong> 1–3 weeks. We coordinate with the sexton on the exact setting appointment.</li>
              <li><strong>First maintenance cleaning:</strong> at six months, included.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>Southern Utah's mild winters are a real cost advantage families do not realize until they compare notes with relatives in northern climates. Cedar City, Enterprise, and higher-elevation cemeteries (Pine Valley, Central, Panguitch) do experience freeze cycles, but St. George Valley itself installs year-round. Northern Utah cemeteries typically freeze from November through March, blocking new installations for four months. We do not have that constraint in Washington County.</p>
          </div>

