            <h2>9. After installation — what to expect</h2>
            <p>Southern Utah headstone maintenance is different from northern climates in three specific ways:</p>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>First cleaning at six months.</strong> Included in every installation we do. Removes any first-season hard-water spotting and confirms the setting is stable.</li>
              <li><strong>Ongoing cadence.</strong> Gentle non-ionic cleaning every 18–24 months on polished granite. Every 12 months on lighter or salt-and-pepper stones. Never on marble in the desert (which is why we don't sell marble).</li>
              <li><strong>Decoration rules.</strong> Every Washington County cemetery has different decoration rules that change seasonally. Tonaquint's fence rule changed on 16 January 2026. Hurricane, Ivins, and Santa Clara each have their own. Check the individual cemetery guide before adding permanent decorations.</li>
